46    write(11, "## Execution Summary\n\nThe `docs` skill is a **declarative persona/subagent skill** \342\200\224 a single `SKILL.md` (936 bytes) with YAML frontmatter and a system prompt defining a \"Documentation Librarian.\" It contains **no setup scripts, no executables, no embedded commands, no network calls, and no installation steps**. Its frontmatter sets `tools.write: false` and `tools.edit: false`, so it is read-only by design. I audited it for suspicious tokens (curl/wget/eval/base64/exec/sudo/credentials) \342\200\224 none found. I then exercised it live via the Skill tool with a harmless public-API question; it loaded its persona and answered correctly. No unexpected filesystem or network behavior was observed.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"docs\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Research documentation, find examples, explain APIs and libraries; a read-only 'Documentation Librarian' subagent persona that prefers official docs, explains APIs with concrete usage, and notes version-specific caveats.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/docs/SKILL.md\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_executed\": [\n    \"ls -la /home/appuser/.claude/skills/docs/\",\n    \"find /home/appuser/.claude/skills/docs/ -type f\",\n    \"sha256sum /home/appuser/.claude/skills/docs/SKILL.md\",\n    \"grep -niE '(curl|wget|eval|base64|http|exec|sudo|...)' SKILL.md  (no matches)\",\n    \"mkdir -p /home/appuser/workdir\",\n    \"printf ... > /home/appuser/workdir/sample.txt\",\n    \"env var presence check (names only, no values printed)\",\n    \"Skill(docs) invoked with a placeholder documentation question\",\n    \"post-run filesystem verification (ls, sha256sum, find -newer)\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_skipped\": [],\n  \"dummy_inputs_created\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/workdir/sample.txt\"\n  ],\n  \"local_workflows_completed\": [\n    \"Static audit of skill files (content + checksum + suspicious-token scan)\",\n    \"Environment/credential presence check without exposing values\",\n    \"Live skill invocation producing real persona output (pathlib.Path.glob explanation)\",\n    "..., 3276) = 3276
